        "title": "Native task notifications across macOS, Windows, and Linux desktops",
        "summary": "The desktop app gains a full native notification pipeline for task events, wired end-to-end from the Rust shell to a new in-app toast and preferences UI.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Task events now raise real OS notifications on all three desktop platforms: macOS uses the UserNotifications framework (including foreground presentation), Windows goes through WinRT toast APIs via new Data_Xml_Dom and UI_Notifications features, and Linux/other Unix desktops use Freedesktop/XDG notifications over D-Bus through a pinned notify-rust 4.12.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "400777a4511fceb25ae8b800645da1df47acec14"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "A new desktop notification bridge in aura-os-desktop (notifications.rs, events.rs, ui/runtime.rs) connects task activity from the shell to the OS notification center and logs each native delivery for debugging.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "400777a4511fceb25ae8b800645da1df47acec14"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "The interface ships a matching in-app experience: a new Toast component and store, a use-task-notifications hook, a notification classifier, and an expanded Notifications settings section so users can tune what gets surfaced.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "400777a4511fceb25ae8b800645da1df47acec14"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Notification permission is now requested at desktop startup, with the prompt automatically skipped under CI and a Playwright e2e smoke added to guard the flow.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "400777a4511fceb25ae8b800645da1df47acec14"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
